{"id": "unknown-2026-07-24-008", "date": "2026-07-24", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 30, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Apple and other smartphone makers pressure OLED producers to reduce costs, some look into utilizing lower-resolution panels", "content": "<p>Component costs are rising - <a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/memory-shortage-may-have-more-implications-oled-industry-valve-admits-it-cannot\">memory prices have been high for a while</a>, and now other component vendors are also raising prices. One example is Qualcomm that announced yesterday that it is raising its chip prices by \"double digits\". This puts a strong pressure on device makers, including smartphone makers, to try and find ways to cut costs in other components.</p><img data-en", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/apple-and-other-smartphone-makers-pressure-oled-producers-reduce-costs-some", "type": "rss"}]}
